    },
    {
      "sentence": "It does not specify which real data to use, what metrics to report, or how to design the evaluation.",
      "error_type": "evidence_misread",
      "explanation": "The scoring criteria do not require the comment to specify these low-level details for an action to be concrete, so this is a misrepresentation of what is needed to meet the 5-point rubric standard."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "The authors know they need to add an empirical evaluation, but they do not know exactly how to carry it out.",
      "error_type": "factual_error",
      "explanation": "The comment clearly defines what modification is needed, so authors do know exactly what action to take. Unspecified minor implementation details do not make the action itself unclear."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "Therefore, the comment is explicit but vague, fitting the description for a score of 3.",
      "error_type": "score_mapping_error",
      "explanation": "The comment meets all rubric criteria for a score of 5 (explicit, concrete action authors can implement directly), so the mapping of the reasoning to a score of 3 is incorrect."
    }
  ],
  "overall_basis": "The rationale incorrectly requires unnecessary low-level implementation details that are not mandated by the scoring rubric, leading to an incorrect score assignment that contradicts the gold label, so it supports the wrong score."
